# Domain architecture

Fix the law, not the symptom. Do not add one-off checks, special-case IDs, or extra files that paper over a broken rule.

## Layers (keep these; do not add parallel copies)

- `lib/domain/models/` — bottles, layers, levels, objectives
- `lib/domain/rules/` — PourRules, BlockerRules, WinRules (the only game laws)
- `lib/domain/engine/` — PuzzleEngine session only; it must call rules, not reimplement them
- `lib/domain/solver/` — LevelSolver uses the same rules as live play
- `lib/domain/levels/` — LevelQa (one ship door), LevelCatalog, onboard levels
- `lib/domain/generator/` — BoardScrambler + LevelGenerator (reverse-from-solved)

## Ship door

A vial ships only if `LevelQa` says so: legal color counts, no leftover extras, crystal lids can crack, not already sorted, and the solver finds a real win of at least `GameConfig.minPlayableMoves(id)` pours.

Live play win = `WinRules.meetsWin`. Solver win = the same method. Never a second definition.

## Generation

Build from a solved board, scramble until unsorted, then apply mechanics. Never emit a pre-solved board or a layout the QA door would reject.

## Examples

```dart
// BAD — patch around vial 16 / 22 / 31
if (level.id == 31) scrambleAgain();
if (bottle.id == 0) bottle.crystal = false;

// GOOD — the rule forbids the class of bug
if (WinRules.isBoardSorted(bottles)) reject;
if (!LevelQa.isPlayable(level)) do not ship;
```
